 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "A book for «القرآن». 103-104 under a night sky: no animals (bahira, sa'iba…), no idols drawn. The ear-cutting definitions are not glossed. Their saying «حسبنا ما وجدنا عليه آباءنا» is glossed only with As-Sa'di's rebuttal. STAGING v4: 101: believers in a town who do not ask; book plate and reading on 101:17 (the Quran), they bow on 101:20 (Allah pardoned it) and leave on 101:22; geometric on the Name (101:23). Nobody is shown asking the Messenger, and nobody faces an empty side. 102: a people of the past (unnamed, at most 3 figures) appear on 102:1, turn on 102:7 and shake their heads on 102:9 (they asked, then rejected it: both tafsirs). 103-104 stay ambient (night sky): the pagan livestock customs and rites cannot be drawn, and 104 is about people invited to the Messenger."
 },
